{
  "as_of": "2026-10",
  "about": "Nominal, manufacturer-published camera specifications used for planning estimates. `min_interval_s` is the shortest reliable still-photo interval; null means it is not published and the planner assumes a conservative default. Sensor dimensions are the active image area: where a manufacturer publishes only a format name (4/3-inch, 1/2.3-inch) they are derived from the lens focal length and its published 35 mm equivalent, which is what makes the computed ground resolution agree with the vendor's own figures. `wpml.payload_enum` is the DJI WPML payload id; `source` says where it comes from (dji-docs = DJI's published tables, community = reported from native route files, not in DJI's public documentation).",
